 },
 "note": "12 Nov, the owner: new lessons written with sharper prompts (aimed at what every Bob got wrong in the 12 Nov benchmark: tools on plain chat, exact arguments, long jobs; plus code fixing, recovering, clarifying, research), each graded by the teacher (--review, failures kept apart in rejected.jsonl) and never repeating a request already in a lesson folder (--avoid). Then the trained Qwen (Bobert, the same teacher as the 24,158 lessons already scored on 10 Nov) scores ONLY these new lessons: the base lesson set (out/lessons-none) is empty, so the odds cover just what was missing. About 5 h writing + 1 h odds on an H200, caps 8 h / $45. | 12 Nov, the owner: lesson sets for the four Famous styles in the Lab's thinking paths (Sherlock Fable-like, Watson Opus-like, Vulcan GPT-like, Raider DeepSeek-like), 400 each, thinking on for every turn so tool turns carry the style too. Taught as a switch: the saved lessons carry only 'Think: <name>' in the system prompt; the style text (forge/plans/think-*.txt) is shown to the teacher only. Written by Bob's own teacher, never from those models' answers. | 12 Nov (later): plus twins (tool / no-tool pairs on one topic), missed (the plain requests the benchmark showed Bob gets wrong) and default (vague asks with one sensible default: do it and say which); agent and recover now think on every turn. 7,000 lessons, H200 only (no B200 step-up) so the run stays inside $70, about 10.5 h.",
